# ===========================================================================
# .env.example - the ANCHOR's environment, and NOTHING ELSE
# (stack-layers L.2 / D10, 2026-09-19)
# ===========================================================================
# THE RULE (D10): a variable lives in the .env of the PLANE whose service reads
# it. This file - the root one - keeps only what is read by the anchor
# (docker-compose.yml), by the stack driver (scripts/stack/stack.py), or by a
# script that is NOT plane-scoped. A plane variable appearing here is drift.
#
# THE PLANE FILES, each loaded NATIVELY by compose from its own project
# directory (no `--env-file`, from any working directory):
#
#   frontend/.env.example    openwebui + tailscale + their backups
#   inference/.env.example   llama.cpp upstreams + llm-queue + LiteLLM gateway
#   memory/.env.example      mnemory + cloud gateway + backup
#   search/.env.example      Mullvad vpn + redis + searxng + gateway
#   coder/.env.example       open-terminal + little-coder + lc-egress + backup
#   portal/.env.example      the internet front-end (portal-on.ps1)
#   agent-org/docker/.env.example   Mattermost + the governed agent-bridge org
#   OB1/docker/.env          Open Brain (a SUBMODULE; see the note at the end)
#
# COPY THIS FILE TO `.env`, AND EACH PLANE EXAMPLE TO ITS OWN `<plane>/.env`.
# The root .env must still EXIST even though it is nearly empty: the anchor
# project's directory is the repo root, so compose (and the driver's `doctor`)
# looks for it there.
#
# COMPOSE_PROFILES is NOT here any more (D17). It was one global assignment
# back when every plane was driven with `--env-file .env` and therefore read
# the same value. Now each project loads its own file, so the variable lives in
# each plane's own .env carrying only that plane's profiles - `stock` in
# frontend/.env, a commented `local` in inference/.env, and deliberately none
# in portal/.env. The anchor declares no services and no profiles, so it has
# none.
#
# MIGRATING AN EXISTING DEPLOYMENT: documentation/runbooks/env-split-migration.md
# lists every variable that used to be here, its source line in the pre-split
# file, and its destination - in an order that never leaves the running stack
# without a value. That runbook is the ONLY place the migration happens; the
# commit that introduced this file deployed nothing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NAS off-site backup credentials (2026-09-13)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT plane-scoped, which is why they are still here: the dedicated Synology
# backup-only SMB user is used by the WEEKLY off-site sync,
# scripts/backup/backup-to-nas.ps1 (scheduled task 'AI-Stack Portal NAS
# Backup'), which sweeps EVERY plane's snapshots. Real values live in the
# gitignored .env.
#
# Synology EXPIRES this password on a schedule. When it does, `net use` fails
# with system error 2242 and the weekly sync stops - it did exactly that
# between 2026-08-30 and 2026-09-13, missing two runs. To rotate:
#   1. set the new password on the NAS (DSM > Control Panel > User)
#   2. put it in .env as NAS_BACKUP_PASSWORD
#   3. powershell -File scripts/backup/set-nas-credential.ps1 -FromEnv
#      (re-seals secrets/nas-backup-vault.dat, the DPAPI fallback store)
# The script reads .env FIRST and the vault only as a fallback, so step 3 is
# for keeping the two in step - not required for the next run to work.
NAS_BACKUP_USER=backup-user
NAS_BACKUP_PASSWORD=change-me-see-comment-above

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# M.8 T2 validation profile
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT plane-scoped either: `scripts/issue-ops/issue_ops.py t2` builds an
# ephemeral twin of a service on ANY plane and passes this file's `.env.test`
# sibling alongside that plane's own env file. The real value lives in the
# gitignored .env.test (created via the J.1 /key/generate flow, alias
# test-validation): the low-priority gateway lane for those twins. Copy this
# line there with the minted key:
TEST_VALIDATION_LLM_KEY=sk-change-me-test-validation

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHERE THE REST WENT - names only, so a search for one lands somewhere
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every variable below used to be assigned in this file and now lives in the
# plane file named beside it. The full table, with the pre-split line number of
# each, is documentation/runbooks/env-split-migration.md.
#
#   frontend/.env   OWUI_IMAGE, WEBUI_SECRET_KEY, OWUI_CHAT_LLM_API_KEY,
#                   GPU_AISTACK_DEVICE_ID, ENABLE_CODE_INTERPRETER,
#                   ENABLE_CODE_EXECUTION, ENABLE_WEB_SEARCH,
#                   WEB_SEARCH_ENGINE, SEARXNG_QUERY_URL, TAILSCALE_AUTH_KEY,
#                   LLAMA_CPP_{ENABLED,HOST,PORT}, LLAMA_CPP_EMBED_{...},
#                   OPEN_NOTEBOOK_{ENABLED,HOST,PORT,TS_PORT,API_PORT,API_TS_PORT},
#                   QUARTZ_{ENABLED,HOST,PORT,TS_PORT},
#                   OPENWEBUI_BACKUP_{RETAIN_COUNT,INTERVAL},
#                   TAILSCALE_BACKUP_{RETAIN_COUNT,INTERVAL}
#   inference/.env  GPU_LLAMA_CPP_DEVICE_ID, GPU_LLAMA_CPP_EMBED_DEVICE_ID,
#                   LM_MODELS_DIR, LLAMA_CPP_CACHE_TYPE_{K,V},
#                   LLAMA_CPP_TIMEOUT, LLAMA_ARG_CTX_CHECKPOINTS,
#                   LLAMA_SWAP_QWEN36_35B_*, LLAMA_SWAP_QWEN36_27B_*,
#                   LLM_QUEUE_*, LITELLM_DB_PASSWORD, LITELLM_MASTER_KEY,
#                   LITELLM_UI_{MASTER_KEY,USERNAME,PASSWORD},
#                   LITELLM_BACKUP_RETAIN_DAYS, OPENROUTER_API_KEY,
#                   LM_MODELS_BACKUP_*
#   memory/.env     MCP_API_KEY, MCP_API_KEYS, MNEMORY_LLM_API_KEY,
#                   MNEMORY_LLM_CONTEXT_SIZE, MNEMORY_GATEWAY_KEY,
#                   MNEMORY_CLOUD_USER, BACKUP_RETAIN_COUNT,
#                   MNEMORY_BACKUP_INTERVAL
#   search/.env     GATEWAY_API_KEY, SEARXNG_SECRET_KEY,
#                   MULLVAD_WG_{PRIVATE_KEY,ADDRESSES}, MULLVAD_COUNTRIES,
#                   SEARCH_NET_SUBNET, SEARXNG_IMAGE, SEARCH_REDIS_IMAGE,
#                   VPN_IMAGE, and the seven NOT-WIRED gateway tunables
#                   (PROVIDER_PRIORITY, CACHE_TTL_SECONDS,
#                   REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, CIRCUIT_FAILURE_THRESHOLD,
#                   CIRCUIT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS, LOG_LEVEL, LOG_QUERIES), which
#                   search/.env.example now ships COMMENTED OUT because nothing
#                   injects them into the gateway container
#   coder/.env      OPEN_TERMINAL_API_KEY, LITTLE_CODER_VERSION, LC_ROUTE_EXEC,
#                   LC_LLAMA_API_KEY, LC_DEPLOY_TOKEN, LC_BACKUP_RETAIN_COUNT,
#                   LITTLE_CODER_BACKUP_INTERVAL, LC_SELF_REMOTE_URL,
#                   LC_SELF_REMOTE_PAT
#   portal/.env     PUBLIC_DOMAIN, ACME_EMAIL, CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN,
#                   AUTHELIA_{JWT_SECRET,SESSION_SECRET,STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY},
#                   WORKBENCH_KEY, DIGEST_{TO,FROM,WINDOW_HOURS},
#                   ALERT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN, PORTAL_DIGEST_CRON, TRIPWIRE_CRON,
#                   TUNNEL_WATCHER_{POLL_SEC,FAILURES_BEFORE_ALERT},
#                   CADDY_BACKUP_*, AUTHELIA_BACKUP_*
#
#   OB1/docker/.env POSTGRES_{USER,PASSWORD,DB}, OPENBRAIN_DB_BACKUP_*,
#                   OPENBRAIN_WIKI_BACKUP_*, OPEN_NOTEBOOK_BACKUP_*,
#                   OPEN_NOTEBOOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY, OPEN_NOTEBOOK_LLM_API_KEY,
#                   SURREAL_USER, SURREAL_PASSWORD.
#                   These were ALREADY read from OB1's own env file, never from
#                   this one (swept 2026-09-19: their only `${...}` references
#                   are in OB1/docker/docker-compose.yml). They were documented
#                   here and nowhere else, and OB1 is a pinned SUBMODULE this
#                   item may not edit - so `OB1/docker/.env.example` still does
#                   not carry them. That gap is recorded in
#                   documentation/notes/stack-layers-sl-env-split-findings.md
#                   and belongs to a follow-up item in the submodule.
#
# DELETED OUTRIGHT, not moved: BACKUP_INTERVAL, RETAIN_COUNT and MIN_AGE_SECS.
# Those are the CONTAINER-side names. Every sidecar sets them itself in its own
# `environment:` block from a prefixed host variable - e.g.
# `- BACKUP_INTERVAL=${MNEMORY_BACKUP_INTERVAL:-86400}` - so no compose file
# ever interpolated the bare names and setting them here changed nothing. The
# prefixed variables above are the real knobs.
# (Identified by sl-closeout: documentation/notes/stack-layers-sl-closeout-findings.md
# section 3, which handed them to this item.)
